# Data contract: what each figure and table reads

`experiment-repo` (analysis) supplies result tables; `figtab-repo` draws them. One tidy CSV per item, UTF-8,
header row, one row per (dataset x conclusion x ...) as below. Every row carries enough to say what it was
computed on. Columns marked * are required; extra columns are ignored by the plotting code.

Common columns (every file):
- `dataset`* short id (e.g. `arena55k`, `arena55k_gpt4judge`, `mtbench_human`, `mtbench_gpt4`, `nba_2005`)
- `design`* one of `crowd`, `expert`, `llm_judge`, `sports` (extra values allowed, they get a neutral colour)
- `synthetic`* 0/1; synthetic rows are drawn hollow / hatched and labelled in the legend
- `N`* comparisons after preprocessing (ties counted as stated in the paper)
- `cost_unit`, `perturbation` (`delete`|`flip`|`insert`), `seed_set`, `n_boot` (kept for provenance, shown in appendix)

