Fig. 1 draws pairs inside the declared z range [1, 8] only (`z_fisher`); the equivalence band is exp(+-0.15), copied from the
pre-analysis note into `margins.json`. Table 2 takes `--datasets` and `--family` for the main-text subset and always also writes `tab2_full_delete.tex` and `tab2_full_flip.tex`.

Rules I hold myself to: uncertainty is drawn only from the `lo`/`hi` columns supplied (no intervals computed in
the plotting code); axis ranges are never clipped silently (values outside are reported by the generator);
a row with `synthetic=1` is never drawn without the synthetic marker. A file that is missing means the figure
is not built; I do not substitute.
Each generator `make_figN.py` takes `--data DIR --out DIR` and writes `figN.pdf` plus `figN.provenance.json`
(input file sha256, row counts, rows dropped and why).

